\ mandelbrot, parallel — pmap-reduce variant of pyperformance/mandelbrot.h2o.
\ Rows are independent, so each row's in-set pixel count is computed on a worker
\ (num-cores workers over the shared heap) and the counts are summed. The sum is
\ order-independent, so the checksum is identical to the serial version.

1000 constant n
50 constant max-iter

: in-set? ( cr ci -- flag )
  | >cr >ci zr zi zr2 zi2 iter |
  0.0 to zr  0.0 to zi  0 to iter
  begin iter max-iter < while
    zr zr f* to zr2
    zi zi f* to zi2
    zr2 zi2 f+ 4.0 f> if leave then
    zr zi f* 2.0 f* ci f+ to zi
    zr2 zi2 f- cr f+ to zr
    f++ iter
  repeat
  iter max-iter >= ;

: render-row ( y -- count )
  | >y ci count x |
  y 2.0 f* n f/ 1.0 f- to ci
  0.0 to count  0 to x
  begin x n < while
    x 2.0 f* n f/ 1.5 f- ci in-set? if f++ count then
    f++ x
  repeat
  count ;

now to t0
n iota 0.0 ' render-row [: f+ :] pmap-reduce to checksum
now t0 - to elapsed
"elapsed: " . elapsed . " s" . cr
"checksum: " . checksum . cr
bye
